                <pb facs="0148" n="128" xml:id="pg128"/>

                <head>[From Galignani]</head>
                <p>A letter from Calais states that the confederate vessel the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rappahannock,</hi> at present in that port, lately had a
                    judgment pronounced against her by the Chamber of Commerce of Boulogne, for
                    commercial debts of the captain. It appears that when the huissier, charged to
                    affix the notice of sale, made his appearance on board the vessel, the captain
                    warned him off without delay, as no such errand should be performed there. The
                    huissier had nothing else to do but to retire, and draw up a proces-verbal of
                    the circumstance.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Vigre de Cherbourg</hi> announces that the
                    confederate vessel <hi rendition="#italic">General Lee</hi> has received orders
                    to be in the channel by the 15th instant.</p>
            </div>
